# errors.log

Purpose:
Record crashes, repeated loops, tool failures, model failures, failed commands, corrupted outputs, or anything that blocked progress.

This file is for operational failures, not normal public test failures. Normal score progression belongs in test_runs.log.

Format:

[YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM] ERROR
Type:
What happened:
Impact:
Action taken:
Resolved: yes/no

Examples:

[2026-05-21 20:39] ERROR
Type: MODEL_TIMEOUT
What happened: Local model request timed out during spec summarization.
Impact: Agent loop stopped before writing implementation plan.
Action taken: Restarted model server and reran the same prompt.
Resolved: yes

[2026-05-21 21:48] ERROR
Type: LOOP_STUCK
What happened: Agent applied nearly identical parser patch four times with no score improvement.
Impact: Public score stayed at 91/250 for 45 minutes.
Action taken: Human edited prompt to force failure-category analysis before next patch.
Resolved: yes

[2026-05-22 00:27] ERROR
Type: BAD_OUTPUT
What happened: Agent added debug prints to stdout, causing JSON parsing failures.
Impact: Previously passing CLI tests failed.
Action taken: Agent was instructed to remove all debug stdout and rerun CLI tests.
Resolved: yes

[2026-05-22 03:12] ERROR
Type: TOOL_FAILURE
What happened: Test runner path was stale after repository structure changed.
Impact: Agent could not run public tests.
Action taken: Updated agent config path. Logged intervention separately in human_interventions.log.
Resolved: yes

